{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":1057,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Lam.1","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Lamentations","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Lamentations 1","reference":"Lamentations 1","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"Jeremiah laments the former excellency and present misery of Jerusalem for her sin, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-11.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"She complains of her grief, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"12-17.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Confesses God's judgments to be righteous: and prays to him, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"18-22.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":8,"text":"A widow - She that had a king, or rather a God, that was an husband to her, now was forsaken of God, and her king taken from her.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":9,"text":"3.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Because - Because of the servitude and oppression exercised among them: oppression by their rulers, and servitude more generally; keeping their servants beyond the year of jubilee, when they ought to be set at liberty.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"The straits - Those that pursued them overtook them in places where they could not escape.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":13,"text":"She - Persons of all ages and ranks are in bitterness.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":14,"text":"10.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":15,"text":"Pleasant things - Has laid violent hands on them.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":16,"text":"The things of the sanctuary were always pleasant things to those that feared God.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":10,"scriptureVerseEnd":10},{"verse":17,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":18,"text":"Bread - Even in a land that ordinarily flowed with milk and honey, they were at a loss for bread to eat.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":19,"text":"Given - And gave any thing for something to satisfy their hunger.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":20,"text":"Vile - Miserable or contemptible.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":21,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":22,"text":"Is it nothing - The prophet speaks in the name of the Jewish church.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":23,"text":"13.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":24,"text":"Fire - A judgment as consuming, and afflictive as fire.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":13,"scriptureVerseEnd":13},{"verse":25,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":26,"text":"Is bound - Put upon my neck on account of my transgressions.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":27,"text":"Wreathed - My punishments are twisted as cords; I have a complication of judgments upon me, sword, famine, pestilence, captivity.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":28,"text":"15.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":29,"text":"An assembly - God had called an assembly of Chaldeans against the city, to crush the inhabitants of it.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":30,"text":"Trodden - God had trodden upon the Jews as men use to stamp grapes in a wine- press.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":15,"scriptureVerseEnd":15},{"verse":31,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":32,"text":"The comforter - God.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":33,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":34,"text":"Jerusalem - Is become loathsome and filthy.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":35,"text":"19.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":36,"text":"Deceived - They did not answer my expectation.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":19,"scriptureVerseEnd":19},{"verse":37,"text":"20.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":38,"text":"Death - By famine and pestilence.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":39,"text":"21.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":40,"text":"They - The neighbouring nations.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21},{"verse":41,"text":"Like me - But thou hast foretold their destruction also, and hast by me proclaimed it: and thou shalt in that day bring them into as sad a condition as I am in now.","sourceParagraph":15,"scriptureVerseStart":21,"scriptureVerseEnd":21}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Lamentations","chapter":1}}